### Loan Project — Phase 8 auth/security demo
#
# Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains Rider (click "Send
# Request" above each call). Start the API first: `dotnet run --project
# src/LoanProject.Api` (default profile serves http://localhost:5213).
#
# Requests are chained: run each named login once, then the requests below reuse
# its token automatically. Easiest is to send top-to-bottom.
#
# Seeded dev credentials are non-secret local defaults (same class as
# appsettings.Development.json). Real deployments use Vault.

@base = http://localhost:5213
@password = Dev!Passw0rd

# ==================================================================
# A. Role-based access control: 401 (no token) / 403 (wrong role) / 200
# ==================================================================

### A1 — no token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{base}}/reports/portfolio-summary

### A2 — log in as a customer (somsri)
# @name loginCustomer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "somsri", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A3 — customer hits a back-office report -> 403 Forbidden
GET {{base}}/reports/portfolio-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.access_token}}

### A4 — log in as admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A5 — admin hits the report -> 200 OK
GET {{base}}/reports/portfolio-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ==================================================================
# B. MFA / OTP second factor (the "officer" login has MFA enabled)
# ==================================================================

### B1 — password step -> { mfaRequired: true, mfaToken }; the 6-digit code is
###      printed in the running app's console (and Seq), not returned here.
# @name loginOfficer
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "officer", "password": "{{password}}" }

### B2 — copy the code from the app log into otpCode, then send B3.
@otpCode = 757102

### B3 — exchange the MFA token + code for a real access token
POST {{base}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mfaToken": "{{loginOfficer.response.body.$.mfaToken}}", "code": "{{otpCode}}" }

# ==================================================================
# C. Field-level encryption + masking
# ==================================================================

### C1 — onboard a customer with PII (LoanOfficer/Admin only)
# @name createCustomer
POST {{base}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{ "fullName": "Demo Person", "nationalId": "1234512345123", "bankAccountNumber": "123-4-56789-0" }

### C2 — read it back -> nationalId/bankAccountNumber come masked (last 4 only).
###      Ciphertext-at-rest: check the SQL column directly.
###      Log masking: find "Customer onboarded" in Seq (http://localhost:5341).
GET {{base}}/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ==================================================================
# D. OAuth 2.0 client-credentials (system-to-system)
# ==================================================================

### D1 — machine client obtains a token (form-encoded, per the OAuth spec)
# @name clientToken
POST {{base}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=loan-report-bot&client_secret=dev-oauth-client-secret-change-me

### D2 — the System token may read reports -> 200
GET {{base}}/reports/portfolio-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ==================================================================
# E. IDOR: a customer may read only their own records
# ==================================================================

### E1 — somsri reads her own customer record -> 200
GET {{base}}/customers/5eed0000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.access_token}}

### E2 — log in as a different customer (somchai)
# @name loginOther
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "somchai", "password": "{{password}}" }

### E3 — somchai tries to read somsri's record -> 404 (existence not leaked)
GET {{base}}/customers/5eed0000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOther.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ==================================================================
# F. Loan lifecycle + KYC gate — actor taken from the token, not the body
# ==================================================================

### F1 — a customer cannot originate a loan -> 403
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.access_token}}

{ "customerId": "5eed0000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "principal": 50000, "rateType": "Effective", "termMonths": 12 }

### F2 — admin originates a loan for the customer created in C1 (still KYC Pending) -> 201
# @name originate
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{ "customerId": "{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}", "principal": 50000, "rateType": "Effective", "termMonths": 12 }

### F3 — approval is blocked by the KYC gate -> 422 (customer is not Verified yet)
POST {{base}}/loans/{{originate.response.body.$.loanId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ==================================================================
# G. KYC — locked to the Compliance policy
# ==================================================================

### G1 — a customer cannot change KYC -> 403 (compliance-only)
PUT {{base}}/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}/kyc
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.access_token}}

{ "status": "Verified" }

### G2 — log in as a compliance officer
# @name loginCompliance
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "compliance", "password": "{{password}}" }

### G3 — compliance verifies the customer -> 204
PUT {{base}}/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}/kyc
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCompliance.response.body.$.access_token}}

{ "status": "Verified" }

### G4 — approval now passes -> 204. approvedBy + ApprovedByUserId come from the
###      token (no ApprovedBy in the body). Check the EventStore row afterwards.
POST {{base}}/loans/{{originate.response.body.$.loanId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### G5 — admin disburses (payment-path) -> 204. DisbursedByUserId from the token.
POST {{base}}/loans/{{originate.response.body.$.loanId}}/disburse
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ==================================================================
# H. AML — a large principal raises a review flag (Mongo auditLog), non-blocking
# ==================================================================

### H1 — admin originates a large loan -> 201; check Mongo "auditLog" for AmlReviewFlagged
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{ "customerId": "5eed0000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002", "principal": 5000000, "rateType": "Effective", "termMonths": 12 }
